<article class="legal-content">
    <p class="legal-updated">Effective date: November 25, 2026</p>
    <p>BLife PH helps members and participating healthcare facilities publish blood requests, donation offers, and related community information. This notice describes information the current platform stores and how its features use it. The platform operator's verified legal name and privacy contact are not configured in this project; publish those details before using this as a production notice.</p>

    <h3>Information collected and stored</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Account and profile:</strong> email address, password hash, first and last name, phone number, blood type, province, donor-search choice, and privacy preferences.</li>
        <li><strong>Posts and participation:</strong> community posts, donation offer details, blood type and availability, request details including blood type, units, urgency, facility/location and needed date, responses, comments, interactions, saved posts, notifications, and messages.</li>
        <li><strong>Location:</strong> the province and city/municipality selected for a profile or post. Blood request and donation offer map coordinates are stored with posts when provided. The map API rounds public marker coordinates to two decimal places; post content and displayed location details may still identify a facility or place. Do not use a private home address as a posting location.</li>
        <li><strong>Account security:</strong> login session hashes, browser user-agent text, session timestamps, and email-change verification token hashes. Passwords are stored as password hashes, not readable passwords.</li>
        <li><strong>Facility information:</strong> for administrator-created clinic and blood bank accounts, facility identity, contact and representative details, and facility activity associated with the account.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Blood type and blood-request details can reveal health-related information. Do not submit patient records, test results, diagnoses, or other sensitive medical details unless you are authorized and the feature requires them.</p>

    <h3>How information is used and shared</h3>
    <p>BLife PH uses submitted information to operate accounts, show posts and donor-search results according to their settings, connect requesters and potential donors, provide messages and notifications, support facility workflows, and allow administrators to moderate and secure the platform. Relevant information is visible to signed-in members, authorized clinics, or administrators when needed by the feature. Email and phone are not displayed in donor-search results. Donor directory participation and its displayed profile fields are controlled in Settings &amp; Privacy.</p>
    <p>Location search uses the profile's province-level location when enabled. Published blood requests and donation offers have their own post locations and visibility; changing profile privacy settings does not rewrite those posts. The map uses OpenStreetMap tiles, so when a signed-in map is used, the tile provider receives the network request needed to deliver map images. Email verification messages are sent using the site's configured mail service.</p>
    <p>BLife PH does not state that it sells member data. Information may be disclosed where required to respond to a valid legal process or protect users and platform operations, subject to applicable requirements.</p>

    <h3>Retention and security</h3>
    <p>Passwords are hashed. Session records support viewing and revoking signed-in sessions; email-change links are represented by hashed, time-limited tokens. The project does not define a complete retention schedule or publish a security certification. Posts, messages, notifications, and related records may remain while needed for platform history, safety review, or account relationships. A deletion request is reviewed and does not automatically erase records.</p>

    <h3>Your choices and requests</h3>
    <p>Settings &amp; Privacy lets you change donor-directory visibility and selected public profile fields, manage location discovery, change your password, request an email change after verification, view and revoke other sessions, download available account data, deactivate your account, or submit an account-deletion request. Requests for access, correction, objection, erasure/blocking, or data portability may also be raised with the platform operator, subject to applicable law and record-retention needs.</p>
    <p>The Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173) and its implementing rules may apply to personal-data processing. This notice is not a claim of legal compliance or a substitute for advice from the platform operator's privacy counsel. See the <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph/data-subject-rights/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Privacy Commission's data-subject rights information</a>.</p>

    <h3>Contact and updates</h3>
    <p>A verified privacy contact for the platform operator is not currently configured. Contact the site administrator using the support channel provided to you. This notice may be updated as the system's practices change; the effective date above identifies this version.</p>
</article>
